  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Solve the following for $x$ using an appropriate method.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^2=4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\pm2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2&=4\\\\x&=\\pm2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x^2=4x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=0$ or $x=4$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-4x&=0\\\\x(x-4)&=0\\\\x&=0,\\quad 4\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 13
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$x(x-6)=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=0$ or $x=6$",
          "worked": "By the null factor law, $x=0$ or $x-6=0$. So $x=0$ or $x=6$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$(x-2)^2=25$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-3$ or ${x=7}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x-2)^2&=25\\\\x-2&=\\pm5\\\\x&=-3,\\quad 7\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 13
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$(2x+5)(x-3)=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac52$ or $x=3$",
          "worked": "By the null factor law, $2x+5=0$ or $x-3=0$. So $x=-\\frac52$ or $x=3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 13
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$x^2-3x-4=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-1$ or $x=4$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-3x-4&=0\\\\(x+1)(x-4)&=0\\\\x&=-1,\\quad 4\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 13
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$x^2-x-12=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-3$ or $x=4$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-x-12&=0\\\\(x+3)(x-4)&=0\\\\x&=-3,\\quad 4\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 13
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$2x^2+11x+15=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac52$ or $x=-3$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2x^2+6x+5x+15&=0\\\\2x(x+3)+5(x+3)&=0\\\\(2x+5)(x+3)&=0\\\\x&=-\\tfrac52,\\quad -3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$3x^2+8x-16=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac43$ or $x=-4$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3x^2+12x-4x-16&=0\\\\3x(x+4)-4(x+4)&=0\\\\(3x-4)(x+4)&=0\\\\x&=\\tfrac43,\\quad -4\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-j",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$x+\\dfrac1x=\\dfrac52$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac12$ or $x=2$",
          "worked": "The original equation requires $x\\ne0$. Multiply by $2x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x^2+2&=5x\\\\2x^2-5x+2&=0\\\\(2x-1)(x-2)&=0\\\\x&=\\tfrac12,\\quad 2\\end{align*}$$\nBoth roots are nonzero.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-k",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "k",
        "prompt": "$x^3=x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-1$, $0$ or $1$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^3-x&=0\\\\x(x^2-1)&=0\\\\x(x-1)(x+1)&=0\\\\x&=0,\\ 1\\text{ or }-1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-l",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "l",
        "prompt": "$2x^2+4x-7=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-1\\pm\\frac{3\\sqrt2}{2}$",
          "worked": "Using the quadratic formula with $a=2$, $b=4$ and $c=-7$,\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-4\\pm\\sqrt{4^2-4(2)(-7)}}{2(2)}\\\\x&=\\frac{-4\\pm\\sqrt{72}}{4}\\\\x&=-1\\pm\\frac{3\\sqrt2}{2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-m",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "m",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac4x=\\dfrac x4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\pm4$",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne0$, multiply by $4x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}16&=x^2\\\\x&=\\pm4\\end{align*}$$\nBoth roots are nonzero.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-n",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "n",
        "prompt": "$2x-3=\\dfrac9{2x-3}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=0$ or $x=3$",
          "worked": "The denominator requires $x\\ne\\frac32$. Multiply by $2x-3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(2x-3)^2&=9\\\\2x-3&=\\pm3\\\\2x&=3\\pm3\\\\x&=0,\\quad 3\\end{align*}$$\nBoth roots satisfy the restriction.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-o",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "o",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac6{x-2}-\\dfrac{10}{3x+2}=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-2$ or $x=6$\n\nClear the denominators before factorising.",
          "worked": "The denominators require $x\\ne2$ and $x\\ne-\\frac23$. Multiply by $(x-2)(3x+2)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}6(3x+2)-10(x-2)&=(x-2)(3x+2)\\\\8x+32&=3x^2-4x-4\\\\3x^2-12x-36&=0\\\\x^2-4x-12&=0\\\\(x+2)(x-6)&=0\\\\x&=-2,\\quad 6\\end{align*}$$\nBoth roots satisfy the restrictions.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
  },
